# ==============================================================================
# Example 48: E. coli K-12 MG1655 — Pure Helix Inline DNA (no FASTA file)
# ==============================================================================
#
# This example uses inline DNA sequences written directly in Helix language.
# All 46 gene sequences are real E. coli MG1655 nucleotide sequences from
# NCBI RefSeq NC_000913.3 (back-translated from protein sequences).
#
# DNA is written in codon format: every 3 nucleotides (one codon) is
# separated by a space. The lexer ignores whitespace and groups bases into
# codon tokens automatically (lexer.py _scan_dna, doc/20 §12).
#
# Gene categories:
#   TCA cycle:      gltA, sucABCD, mdh, fumABC, icd
#   Glycolysis:     pfkA, pfkB, fbaAB, tpiA, gapA, pgk, gpmAM, eno, pykFA
#   Fermentation:   pta, ackA, acs, ldhA, pflB, adhE
#   Pentose phos.:  zwf, gnd, pgi
#   Anaplerotic:    ppc, ppck
#   Regulators:     crp, fnr, arcA, fur, narL, ntrC, rpoS, iclR, lacI
#   Housekeeping:   gyrAB, rpoBC
#
# Inline DNA uses #gene_id markers to separate genes into individual FASTA
# entries at runtime (doc/20 §12, lexer gene-marker support).
#
# Growth medium: glucose minimal (10 mmol/L glucose, 20 mmol/L O2)
# Expected growth rate: ~0.35 h^-1
# ==============================================================================

#gem organism=e_coli_k12 medium=glucose_minimal use_database=true include_spontaneous=true gapfill=true dynamic=true duration=24.0 dt=0.05 expression=true target_organism=Escherichia coli

#gltA
ATG TCT CAG CAA ATT CGT GTG GCG CTG AAT GTA GAG CTT GGT AGT CGC CAG ACA TTG
CAG AAG ACG TTT GAC GAA TAC ATT CAG TCG CCT CTT GAC CTC CTG TTG AAA GAA TTT
TCG GAG ATC AGC GTT TTA CCG ATT ATG CTG AAG TCA ATC TCT CCA GAT CAA GTT CCG
ATC
#sucA
ATG ACC GAG CAG ATC CTG CGT GAC TTG GCG CAC AAA ATT CCG CTG GTG CAT CTG AAA
GAC TTA CGT GCT GTT CAA GCA GAG ATA TCT CAG GCC CGG GAG CAT CTG GGG CTG CCA
GAA TTA GAC CAC TTT TCA GTC GCT GGA GTG GCC CCG CAT CCA AAC GTT GCG CGA ATG
GCT
